# Paths never pushed to the live server by deploy-web.sh.
#
# Three kinds of entry live here:
#   1. Server-owned: must survive an rsync --delete. `.env.local` holds
#      SECURITY_KEY / SECURITY_USER and the Firebase config, is written by hand
#      on the server, and exists nowhere in this repo — losing it takes the
#      whole site down.
#   2. Built or installed on the server: pushing a local copy is at best wasted
#      transfer and at worst a mismatched binary (node_modules is built against
#      the server's Node and libc, not the Mac's).
#   3. Local-only, and actively harmful in a public docroot: the dev HTTPS
#      certificate includes its private key.

# --- server-owned: never overwrite, never delete ---
# The glob matters: step 2 of deploy-web.sh writes .env.local.bak-<date> next to
# it, and a bare `.env.local` entry would let --delete remove the backup in the
# very next step.
.env.local*
node_modules/
.next/

# --- local-only ---
.git/
.deployignore
deploy-web.sh
.vercel/
certificates/
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
.DS_Store
playwright-report/
test-results/
coverage/
*.log
